[1mThe bug:[22m Rust's standard library sets [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m to [38;5;10mSIG_IGN[0m before [38;5;10mmain[0m runs. When stdout's reader was gone, the C program was killed by signal 13 while the Rust program's failed write returned [38;5;10mEPIPE[0m, which [38;5;10mprint_foo[0m discarded ([38;5;10mlet _ = write!(...)[0m), so it exited 0. Fixed by restoring [38;5;10mSIG_DFL[0m for [38;5;10mSIGPIPE[0m at the top of [38;5;10mmain[0m, declaring [38;5;10msignal(2)[0m via [38;5;10mextern "C"[0m rather than adding a crate dependency. This was invisible to every stdin-driven case — it only appears when the consumer of stdout disappears.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
Everything else already matched, including the parts that look like bugs: a failed [38;5;10mscanf[0m silently leaves its destination at [38;5;10m0[0m (empty input prints [38;5;10m0 0 0 0[0m, exit 0, no error path anywhere in this program); the pushed-back offending byte makes one matching failure poison all later conversions, so [38;5;10m1 2 x 4[0m prints [38;5;10m1 2 0 0[0m and never reaches the [38;5;10m4[0m; [38;5;10m%u[0m accepts a sign and wraps, so [38;5;10m-1[0m prints as [38;5;10m3[0m through the 2-bit field; out-of-range values saturate at 64 bits ([38;5;10mLONG_MAX[0m/[38;5;10mLONG_MIN[0m/[38;5;10mULONG_MAX[0m) and only then truncate to 32, while values that do fit in 64 bits truncate instead.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mTests:[22m 32 integration tests in [38;5;10mtranslation/tests/differential.rs[0m, each spawning both binaries as subprocesses and asserting stdout bytes, stderr bytes, and exit status including death by signal. Coverage is enumerated from the C's branches — the bit-field masks, the one-bit [38;5;10mbool[0m, every conversion boundary, signs with no digits, matching failures at each of the four positions, whitespace forms, NUL and high bytes, every truncated prefix of a full input, and ~1,000 fixed-seed random inputs per run.[0m[0m
